<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 27-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 27-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Peter, with 75 mph winds, is near 28.6n/126.5e, moving north at 14 mph. Landfall is expected in Kyushu as Peter turns northeastward during the next 24 hours. Coastal flooding is possible due to storm surge. Wind damage, flooding rain, and mudslides will likely occur in southern Japan, with heavy rain and gusty winds moving into Honshu during Saturday.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
